Falsifies `system_tests::user::revocation_window_tests::a_reclamation_inside_a_slice_leaves_the_slicer_no_slice`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is the tree as it stood until 2026-10-04 (UTC): the patch puts `PageFrame::SLICE` back
to deriving its slice from a source read in a critical section of its own and filing it with
`sched::grant`. `revoke::revoke_region`'s capability pass (the one `MemoryRegion::DESTROY` runs
before handing the pages back) deletes the run between the two, and the slice is filed after it,
naming pages the allocator is about to reuse.

This was the live tree, not an invented break. Milestone 761 (capability lookup off the global
lock) recorded the gap unverified in its `BUGS`; this test is what verified it.

Expected to fail: `assert!(answer < 0, "a SLICE whose run was reclaimed while it was in progress filed a slice in slot {answer} ...")`. Confirmed red on riscv64 on 2026-10-04 (UTC), before the fix existed, and replayed red the same
day against the fixed tree at `revocation_window_tests.rs:297`, the assertion predicted.

**The assertions above the headline stay green under this patch**, which is what makes the red mean
the claim rather than the fixture: the vacuity guard says the thread really was held inside its
delegation, and the premise check says the sweep really did reach that thread's own table.

Nothing here is architecture-specific: the syscall layer, the sweeps and the seam are portable
code, so one patch serves every leg.

diff --git a/kernel/src/syscall/page_frame.rs b/kernel/src/syscall/page_frame.rs
--- a/kernel/src/syscall/page_frame.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/syscall/page_frame.rs
@@ -107,9 +107,10 @@
 pub(super) fn page_frame_slice(slot: u64, first: u64, len: u64) -> Result<i64, Error> {
     // The source is read under the table lock the slice is filed under, so no reclamation sweep
     // falls between the read and the filing (`sched::Delegation`).
+    let src = sched::current_cap(slot).map_err(|_| Error::NoSuchSlot)?;
     #[cfg(feature = "system_tests")]
     crate::delegation_pause::here(); // no lock held
-    let slot = sched::grant_derived(slot, |src| {
+    let copy = (|src: crate::cap::Cap| {
         let Object::PageFrame(phys, count) = src.object else {
             return Err(Error::WrongObject);
         };
@@ -125,7 +126,8 @@
         }
         let base = phys + first * page_frames::FRAME_SIZE;
         Ok(crate::cap::page_frame_run_cap(base, len, src.rights))
-    })?;
+    })(src)?;
+    let slot = sched::grant(copy).map_err(|_| Error::OutOfMemory)?;
     Ok(slot as i64)
 }
 
